 "assumptions": [
  "headingDeg set to 55 (landside front), replacing the dossier placeholder 171.6: the front line in the satellite image runs on bearing 145.",
  "Pier ridge 25 m is the dossier OSM height; the airside photo scales to about 26 m. Wing roof 30 m is estimated from the two landside photos; no source gives it, and model top differs from the 25 m dossier height for this reason.",
  "Elevation bands of the piers are scaled from a single airside photo and applied to every apron side; the two landside ribbon windows from photos of the south-east wing, applied to all landside flanks.",
  "Dossier calls the pylons beige stone and the trusses dark grey; the 2 landside photos show white-tiled pylons with scored diamonds and pale steel, so photo colours were used for those.",
  "Dossier roof grey is kept for fascias only; roof surfaces use the pale colours seen from the satellite.",
  "The north-west wing mirrors the south-east wing: only the south-east wing was photographed. The roof sign and planter are built only on the south-east.",
  "Pylon position 44 m from the tip, its 13 by 8 m plan, column positions and the lattice cell size are estimates from oblique photos.",
  "Central hall roof 21 m, front block 26 m, clerestory 28.6 m: estimates; heights inside the outline are not documented.",
  "Skylight and terrace roofs are tiled textures from the satellite pattern, not individual openings.",
  "Hall curtain walls under the wings, the 18 m movable bridge tunnels and their parked angle are the plainest form consistent with the photos; 15 fixed links come from the footprint stubs.",
  "Kerb canopy depth and height are assumed; low service blocks 7 m and white kerb frames 5 m are read in plan from satellite with guessed heights, and those frames extend past the dossier footprint.",
  "Airside sign: the photo does not show which arm it is on; placed on the south-east arm.",
  "Lettering uses Blender's built-in font; the real typeface is not matched.",
  "Control tower is not part of this model: it stands away from the terminal and the sources disagree on it."
 ]
